From df2350c2ac396ec085500e0dc040ea49ea7c0e7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] parakeet-cpp: bound memory on long recordings

Window the speech-to-text over overlapping pieces cut at the longest pause,
feed the diarizer through the streaming C API so speaker labels stay stable,
and decode WAV in blocks instead of growing a []int. One hour of audio now
peaks near 2.8 GB instead of 7.6 GB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
